SUMMARY:Take-Two Interactive: GTA VI launch
DESCRIPTION:WHAT TO CHECK\nReview scores\, the technical state of the game\
 , and the first sales figure Take-Two announces.\n\nWHERE THE REPORT STOOD
  (11 Oct 2026)\nVerdict: Wait · buy < $126\nPrice then $213 · bear $82.6
  · base $168 · bull $262\nMargin of safety below $126\n\nIF YOU HOLD IT\
 nHold\, but keep the position small enough that a 40% fall would not hurt\
 , and do not add before the launch. The price already assumes a record lau
 nch\, so the reward for being right is small next to the cost of being wro
 ng.\n\nSIGNALS TO ADD\n• Price below about $168 with the launch delivere
 d\n• The online mode launches and recurrent spending grows above the fis
 cal 2026 level of $5.2bn\n• First fiscal 2028 guidance above fiscal 2027
 \n• Net cash reached and share buybacks restarted\n• Insiders buying s
 hares\n\nSIGNALS TO SELL\n• A third delay of GTA VI\n• The online mode
  slips past fiscal 2028 or earns less than GTA Online does now\n• Fiscal
  2028 guidance below fiscal 2027\n• A large acquisition paid for with ne
 w shares\n• Price above about $262 (the bull value) without higher earni
 ngs estimates\n\nAFTERWARDS\nReport: https://turnivor.github.io/investment
